    "cause": "Bevy 0.20 PBR shaders (pbr_fragment.wesl and three others) bind texture/sampler handles with `let`, which WGSL only allows under the optional language extension texture_and_sampler_let. Safari 27.0.1 does not implement it (Chrome does) and rejects the composed pbr_opaque_mesh_pipeline fragment module ('texture_2d<f32>' cannot be used as the type of a 'let'); Bevy's render error handler then quits the app after frame 3. Task 10's 'no console error' was wrong: Bevy logs ERROR via styled console.log, which its reporter did not capture. Full diagnosis: docs/perf/p0-safari-diagnosis.md.",
    "fix": "web/wgsl-compat.js: wraps GPUDevice.createShaderModule when navigator.gpu.wgslLanguageFeatures lacks texture_and_sampler_let and inlines each handle-typed let alias within its block. Inert in Chrome; ?wgsl_compat=1 forces it, ?wgsl_compat=0 disables it.",
    "functional_runs_not_timed": {
      "note": "Full WebGPU tracer active, no load guard; READY with 600 samples and 0 errors each.",
      "strategic mid1200 (instanced)": "p95 17 ms, mean 16.67 ms",
      "strategic entities layout (default gate2000)": "p95 23 ms, mean 21.94 ms, 5 frames over 25 ms"
    },
    "method": "Scratch copy of dist served on 127.0.0.1:8094 by a bounded node server; injected tracer.js (light mode, trace=0, for timed runs) POSTs hexWorld.diag()/state() every second. Safari opened and sized via AppleScript; no Safari setting or preference was changed and Web Inspector was not used.",
    "caveats": [
      "The Darker and Bitwarden Safari extensions are installed and were not disabled.",
      "Canvas is 2992x1774 device px (1496x887 CSS at DPR 2), larger than the Chrome rows' 2560x1440.",
      "Only the tuned shadow rows were timed; mid600, mid1200 and full were not timed in Safari.",
      "Strategic run 3 was re-run: the first attempt's driver reused the run tag across load-guard retries, so after one discarded sample it read the discarded page's diag (p95 18, mean 16.67). The driver now tags each attempt; the replacement (p95 17) is recorded. Strategic run 2's two discards were verified to be separate page sessions, and its recorded figures come from the final one.",
      "web/wgsl-compat.js was optimized (linear scan, rewrite timing) between the first five runs and the strategic run 3 re-run; its WGSL output is byte-identical (checked with cmp on the 75,220-byte PBR fragment module)."
    ],
